nano_zone address layout for arm64 (aarch64 port, task A12)

The nanozone address field widths are guarded on __x86_64 alone, so a guest arm64 compile
hits "Unknown Architecture" and then every NANO_*_BITS is undeclared. darling PR 1753 uses
the identical widths on arm64 (the nanozone lives in the same 64-bit address layout), so the
fix is only to let the guard accept the two arm64 spellings the compiler may use.

--- a/src/nano_zone.h
+++ b/src/nano_zone.h
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@

 /*************          nanozone address field layout        ******************/

-#if defined(__x86_64)
+#if defined(__x86_64) || defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__)
 #define NANO_MAG_BITS			6
 #define NANO_BAND_BITS			17
 #define NANO_SLOT_BITS			4
